
📘 React JS – Forms, Props, useRef & useFormStatus Notes


---

🔹 1. Reusable Input Component (Props)

What

A component that accepts data from parent using props.

Why

Reduce code repetition

Same input design everywhere


Purpose

Create dynamic & reusable UI components

Syntax

const UserInput = (props) => {
  return (
    <input type="text" style={props.style} />
  );
};

export default UserInput;

Usage

<UserInput style={{padding:"10px", width:"200px"}} />


---

🔹 2. Passing Function as Props

What

Passing parent function to child component.

Why

Child component can send data to parent.

Purpose

Parent–Child communication.

function App() {
  const displayName = (name) => {
    alert(name);
  };

  return <User onClick={displayName} />;
}

function User(props){
  return <button onClick={() => props.onClick("Pawan")}>Click</button>;
}


---

🔹 3. useRef Hook (Uncontrolled Component)

What

Directly access input value without state.

Why

No re-render, fast performance.

Purpose

Access DOM element directly.

import { useRef } from "react";

function App(){
  const userRef = useRef();

  const getUser = () => {
    alert(userRef.current.value);
  };

  return (
    <>
      <input type="text" ref={userRef} />
      <button onClick={getUser}>Get User</button>
    </>
  );
}


---

🔹 4. Controlled Component

What

Input controlled by React State.

Why

Live validation, better control.

const [name,setName] = useState("");

<input type="text" value={name} onChange={(e)=>setName(e.target.value)} />


---

🔹 5. Uncontrolled Component

What

Input controlled by DOM using useRef.

Why

Less code, simple forms.

<input type="text" ref={userRef} />


---

🔹 6. useFormStatus Hook (React 19)

What

Tracks form submission status.

Why

Disable button while submitting.

Purpose

Prevent multiple submissions.

import { useFormStatus } from "react-dom";

function SubmitButton(){
  const { pending } = useFormStatus();
  return <button disabled={pending}>{pending?"Submitting...":"Submit"}</button>;
}


