📘 React Advanced Hooks – forwardRef & useFormStatus


---

🔷 PART 1 — forwardRef in React


---

🔹 What is forwardRef?

forwardRef is used to pass ref from parent to child component.

Normally, ref does not work with custom components.


---

🔹 Why we use forwardRef?

Because this is not allowed in React:

<UserInput ref={myRef}/>

Custom components cannot receive ref directly.


---

🔹 Purpose

Focus input from parent

Access child DOM elements

Create reusable input components



---

🔹 Syntax

import { forwardRef } from "react";

const UserInput = forwardRef((props, ref) => {
  return <input type="text" ref={ref} />;
});

export default UserInput;


---

🔹 Example – Focus Input from Parent

import { useRef } from "react";
import UserInput from "./UserInput";

function App(){
  const inputRef = useRef();

  const focusInput = ()=>{
    inputRef.current.focus();
  };

  return(
    <>
      <UserInput ref={inputRef}/>
      <button onClick={focusInput}>Focus Input</button>
    </>
  );
}


---

🔷 PART 2 — useFormStatus Hook (React 19)


---

🔹 What is useFormStatus?

It tracks form submission status.


---

🔹 Why we use it?

Disable button while submitting

Show loading text

Prevent multiple clicks



---

🔹 Purpose

Improves user experience during form submission.


---

🔹 Syntax

import { useFormStatus } from "react-dom";

function SubmitButton(){
  const { pending } = useFormStatus();

  return (
    <button disabled={pending}>
      {pending ? "Submitting..." : "Submit"}
    </button>
  );
}


---

🔹 Example – Async Form Submit

const handleSubmit = async () => {
  await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res,2000));
  console.log("Form Submitted");
};

<form action={handleSubmit}>
  <input type="text" placeholder="Enter Name"/>
  <input type="password" placeholder="Enter Password"/>
  <SubmitButton/>
</form>


---

🔹 Working

pending Value	Meaning

true	Form is submitting
false	Submission finished


